  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most informative first step is to establish a simple, well-understood baseline that will serve as a reference for all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the minimal configuration: a single modality, a single profile, and a linear (PCA) encoder with no learned components. This establishes the performance floor and eliminates confounding from encoder training dynamics, aggregation, or fusion. Subsequent experiments can then cleanly isolate the marginal contribution of each design axis—e.g., switching the RNA encoder to scVI or scGPT (configs 004/007), adding multiprofile + aggregation (configs 002/003), adding an image modality (configs 010/013), or combining modalities (configs 016+). Starting from the simplest reference point maximizes the information gained per experiment under a limited budget, because every future result can be interpreted as a delta from this anchor rather than as an absolute number with no context."
}

